finding: 1. src/core/rendering/image.ts:262-265 silently consumes failures after Promise.all has already rejected. Register two deferred level sources A and B, start one prepareImages, reject A and await its rejection, then reject B without starting another preparation. B's catch from the already-rejected preparation still replaces its stored promise with a resolved promise, although no preparation can report B's error; all subsequent preparations resolve. Independently reproduced by invoking the real prepareImages with two deferred stored promises: first preparation returned A failed, next preparation resolved after B failed. The new tests pass because they report the first failure before registering the second, so they never exercise two distinct failures included in one preparation. This contradicts the no-silently-dropped-failure claim and JSDoc's reporting rule.
